# Convoke (CR 702.51): a creature tapped for it pays {1} or one mana of its color. Three Mox Jets can pay only generic
# mana, so the {W} of {3}{W} is paid by the white Mother of Runes tapped for convoke, and the Mox Pearl, which could
# have paid it, stays untapped. Bot2 controls only a Plains (a land), so there is no legal target (CR 603.3d): the
# trigger is never put on the stack (no target question) and the Tribunal stays on the battlefield.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mother of Runes
Conclave Tribunal
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mother of Runes.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#3.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Conclave Tribunal.Cast(Convoke: Mother of Runes)
! Bot1.Target
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Mox Jet; Mox Jet; Mother of Runes; Conclave Tribunal
Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Tapped = false
Exile.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield = Plains
